From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: give FastRPC an addressable heap

Attaching to the SLPI's sensor process crashes it on an SMMU context fault at
iova 0x1fffff000, stream 0x5a1, which is the first of the FastRPC compute
contexts. That address is above 4 GB and the DSP addresses 32 bits, so it can
never reach it.

The kernel says as much on both DSP channels, as an informational message rather
than an error:

	qcom,fastrpc ...fastrpcglink-apps-dsp: no reserved DMA memory for FASTRPC

The stock device tree carries what is missing: a 16 MB shared-dma-pool with an
allocation range capped at 0xffffffff, which is what keeps FastRPC buffers where
the DSP can see them. Describe the same pool and point the SLPI's FastRPC node
at it.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 27 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -583,11 +583,48 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/ {
+	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * FastRPC heap. The DSPs address 32 bits, so this has to stay
+		 * below 4 GB: without it the allocator hands out an IOVA above
+		 * that and the sensor process faults the SMMU the moment the
+		 * host attaches. The stock device tree carries the same pool,
+		 * 16 MB with the same allocation range.
+		 */
+		fastrpc_mem: fastrpc-shared-pool {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x00000000 0x0 0xffffffff>;
+			size = <0x0 0x01000000>;
+			reusable;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &remoteproc_slpi {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus/hotdog/slpi.mbn";
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&remoteproc_slpi {
+	glink-edge {
+		fastrpc {
+			memory-region = <&fastrpc_mem>;
+
+			/*
+			 * The sensor DSP holds no rights over the heap unless it
+			 * is assigned to it. Without this the hypervisor refuses
+			 * its accesses, and a refused access stalls the
+			 * interconnect rather than faulting.
+			 *
+			 * HLOS, SSC_Q6 and ADSP_Q6, matching what the downstream
+			 * driver assigns this range to.
+			 */
+			qcom,vmids = <0x3 0x5 0x6>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &remoteproc_mpss {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus/hotdog/modem.mbn";
 	status = "okay";
--
2.50.1
